            0.082
          ],
          "content": "Playing with Constructions"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.118,
            0.834,
            0.188
          ],
          "content": "Have you checked what happens to the length XY when X and Y are placed at the same distance away from A and B, respectively? For example, as in the cases like these:"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.157,
            0.205,
            0.79,
            0.334
          ],
          "content": "| Distance of X from A | Distance of Y from B | Length of XY |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| 5 mm | 5 mm |  |\n| 1 cm | 1 cm |  |\n| 1 cm 5 mm | 1 cm 5 mm |  |",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.145,
                0.35,
                0.258,
                0.369
              ],
              "content": "and so on."
            }
          ],
          "image_source": "images/page_12_table_3.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.384,
            0.481,
            0.405
          ],
          "content": "\u0007In each of these cases, observe"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.146,
            0.406,
            0.679,
            0.428
          ],
          "content": "1. how the length XY compares to that of AB and"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.146,
            0.429,
            0.578,
            0.451
          ],
          "content": "2.\t the shape of the 4-sided figure ABYX."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.458,
            0.833,
            0.504
          ],
          "content": "How does the farthest distance between X and Y compare with the length of AC? BD?"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.52,
            0.275,
            0.542
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "嶽 Construct"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.156,
            0.549,
            0.392,
            0.57
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Breaking Rectangles"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.154,
            0.574,
            0.458,
            0.665
          ],
          "content": "Construct a rectangle that can be divided into 3 identical squares as shown in the figure."
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.47,
            0.563,
            0.831,
            0.65
          ],
          "content": "|  |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_12_table_12.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.155,
            0.675,
            0.259,
            0.695
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Solution"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.155,
            0.701,
            0.673,
            0.725
          ],
          "content": "If this seem difficult, let us simplify the problem."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.737,
            0.244,
            0.76
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "嶽 Explore"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.155,
            0.764,
            0.833,
            0.809
          ],
          "content": "What about constructing a rectangle that can be divided into two identical squares? Can you try it?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.154,
            0.812,
            0.833,
            0.859
          ],
          "content": "It is wise to first plan and then construct. But how do we plan? Can you think of a way?"
        },
